          { name: "Assuming an 82-18 Result Reflects a Stable, Durable Coalition", tag: "avoid", why: "An 82-18 partisan result in a district with meaningful demographic diversity (18.75% Hispanic, 7.4% gap, 24.2% renters), an aging population on middle income facing healthcare inflation, and limited college attainment is not a stable floor — it is a current coalition built on particular economic and cultural alignment. The combination of economic stress among older homeowners and the electoral availability of Hispanic, renter, and gap-population constituencies creates conditions where a well-resourced opposition campaign focused on economic anxiety and community presence can erode the current margin significantly. A representative who treats this seat as electorally secure without attending to the material economic concerns of aging voters, the persuadability of Hispanic residents, and the alienation of renter and gap populations will find the next competitive cycle arrives faster than expected." }
