          "Lead with housing affordability and renter stability as the core constituent concern—51.1% renter rate in a district with $46,142 median income means that rent burden, eviction protections, and entry into homeownership are the material quality-of-life issues for more than half the district. Whichever party offers specific, credible solutions on this issue has the foundation for genuine constituent loyalty; abstract rhetoric on either side will not move voters who are navigating monthly housing insecurity.",
          "Engage the Hispanic-majority constituency (53.22%) with economic specificity, not cultural symbolism—Hispanic voters in this income bracket are responding to wages, job quality, and family economic security far more than to demographic representation or cultural positioning. Credible messaging on entry-level job quality, wage growth, and pathways to stable employment will resonate more powerfully than either party's typical outreach approach.",
          "Recognize that the at-large structure creates a winner-take-all dynamic where the top two finishers win both seats—in a 100% Democratic environment, this means the Democratic primary or the general election itself became the decisive contest, and any Republican candidate must run a general-election campaign from the first day, not assume a primary consolidation strategy will suffice. With no incumbent Republican holding either seat, the rebuild requires a unified candidate recruitment and messaging effort, not a fractured primary field."
