          "Engage Hispanic voters on kitchen-table economics rather than identity politics: the 64% Hispanic population is majority working-class and majority young, and their voting behavior in 2024 reflects economic evaluation, not demographic inevitability. Wage policy, union organizing, small business support, and workplace protections are the economic issues that resonate with this constituency; any candidate who defaults to cultural rhetoric instead of concrete economic policy will find themselves speaking past the actual priorities of HD-26's voters.",
