          { name: "Assuming Age & Homeownership Signals Conservative Uniformity", tag: "avoid", why: "The 52-year median age and 83.2% homeownership create an intuitive expectation of social conservatism, but Arizona's affluent suburban districts have consistently demonstrated that high education, professional-class status, and suburban settlement patterns produce voters who prioritize fiscal responsibility, quality governance, and pragmatic problem-solving over ideological consistency. This constituency is capable of supporting candidates and policies outside traditional conservative positioning if they perceive superior governance competence or alignment with their material interests (education quality, healthcare access, water sustainability, tax efficiency). Any representative who campaigns or governs this district as though age and homeownership guarantee ideological uniformity will miss the specific policy engagement that actually drives electoral loyalty among college-educated, affluent suburban voters." }
