          { name: "Neglecting Day-to-Day Constituent Service & Neighborhood Problem-Solving", tag: "avoid", why: "In a young, urban, renter-majority district, voters evaluate representatives based on visible problem-solving on transit reliability, street maintenance, public safety, zoning fairness, and neighborhood quality-of-life issues—not on partisan messaging or abstract policy positioning. A candidate who is invisible on these day-to-day governance issues, or who delegates constituent service, will lose ground to a challenger who demonstrates tangible delivery. This district is won and held by effectiveness, not by partisan identity; an incumbent or challenger who emphasizes partisan messaging over constituent service fundamentally misreads the electoral dynamics." }
