          "Recognize the 35% Republican floor as a real audience, not a lost cause: these voters include both Anglo residents and Hispanic voters whose economic frustrations or specific policy positions make them persuadable. A Democratic incumbent must prevent their defection by delivering on cost-of-living concerns; a Republican challenger gains ground by offering a credible economic alternative that does not rely on immigration enforcement rhetoric.",
